.TH "GLOBAL STATE MANAGEMENT AND EXCEPTION HANDLING." "3" "" "libiter 2.0.1" "libiter manual"
.SH NAME
Global state management and exception handling. \- API reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include <iter/global.h>\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBITER_API void libiter_use_allocator(allocator_t *allocator);\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBITER_API pf_exception_t *libiter_catch(int error);\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBITER_NO_RETURN ITER_API int libiter_throw(
    int code, const char *func, const char *msg
);\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBITER_NO_RETURN ITER_API int libiter_throwf(
    int code, const char *func, const char *fmt, ...
);\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBITER_NO_RETURN ITER_API int libiter_vthrowf(
    int code, const char *func, const char *fmt, va_list args
);\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBITER_NO_RETURN ITER_API int libiter_rethrow(pf_exception_t *e);\fR
.fi
.SH REFERENCE
.SS libiter_use_allocator
.PP
This function sets the default allocator of the library.
.SS libiter_catch
.PP
This function set's up the exception handler for the \fB<pf_exception.h>\fR
exception handling interface. The first call will return \fBNULL\fR, after
which exception\-throwing code can be executed.
.PP
The second return value will represent the emitted exception.
.RS 4
.PP
The global exception stack is thread local.
.RE
.SS libiter_throw
.PP
Emits an exception with given message.
.SS libiter_throwf
.PP
Emits an exception with given formatting.
.SS libiter_vthrowf
.PP
Emits an exception with given formatting.
.SS libiter_rethrow
.PP
Emits the exception \fBe\fR for the next catcher.
.SH ERROR HANDLING
Errors are reported with the codes of
.B enum libiter_error
from
.IR <iter/types.h> .
.B ITER_OK
(0) means success; every other code is a negative value, such as
.B ITER_EINVAL
or
.BR ITER_ENOMEM .
.PP
Functions that document
.B Returns
report the error by returning its code.
.PP
Functions that document
.B Exceptions
(or
.BR Throws )
emit the error through the
.I <pf_exception.h>
interface.
Wrap the call so the exception can be caught with
.BR libiter_catch ()
(see
.BR global (3)),
which returns
.B NULL
on the first call and the emitted exception afterwards.
Functions that return a pointer return
.B NULL
when an exception was emitted, and functions that return an integer return the
error code.
The exception stack is thread local.
